  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Brush a rimmed baking sheet with 1 tbsp of the olive oil.",
    "Pound the chicken cutlets to an even 1/2 inch thickness. Season both sides with the 1 tsp kosher salt.",
    "Set out three shallow dishes. Put the flour in the first, the beaten eggs in the second, and the breadcrumbs mixed with the Parmesan and garlic powder in the third.",
    "Dredge each cutlet in flour, then egg, then the breadcrumb mix. Press so the crumbs stick. Place on the baking sheet and drizzle with the remaining 2 tbsp olive oil.",
    "Bake for 15 minutes, until the crumbs are golden on top.",
    "Spoon about 1/4 cup marinara over each cutlet and top with the mozzarella. Bake 8 to 10 minutes more, until the cheese is melted and the chicken reaches 165 F.",
    "While the chicken bakes, bring the water and 1 tbsp salt to a boil in a large pot. Cook the spaghetti for 9 to 11 minutes, until tender, then drain.",
    "Warm the remaining marinara in the empty pot. Toss in the spaghetti.",
    "Serve each cutlet over a pile of spaghetti. Cool leftovers fully before freezing the chicken and pasta in separate containers."
  ],
